": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LKQGdZ4jEU94Hkd5wrnMpZ", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 408138, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LKQGdZ4jEU94Hkd5wrnMpZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 411994, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the nightly build failed.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 to confirm the requirement, but the advisory tool doesn't recognise that ID. The fix goes by the test and the docstring instead.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YHbdrbznLCwccJT3eNJ6mS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ac4ruHLfvFsH7aW3Sndugp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011fpJwmfdwZ1gG4W4ybMPHk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"st